cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. Author list to be confirmed."
title: "websemantic: a software-agnostic semantic layer from human intent to qualified simulated data"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Cyril"
    family-names: "Voyant"
    affiliation: "Mines Paris, PSL University, Centre for Observation, Impacts, Energy (O.I.E.), Sophia-Antipolis, France"
    email: "cyril.voyant@minesparis.psl.eu"
    website: "https://person.cyrilvoyant.com"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0242-7377"
url: "https://www.cyrilvoyant.com"
license: "MIT"
version: "0.0.1"
date-released: "2026-10-03"
abstract: >
  Research prototype of a non-intrusive semantic layer that turns natural-language
  requests into traceable, validated configurations of existing scientific
  simulators, runs them unmodified, and publishes their outputs as self-describing
  records with provenance, accepted assumptions, uncertainty coverage and admitted
  uses. Case studies: Tunnel Load Simulator, LQL-Equiv and pvlib-python.
keywords:
  - semantic web
  - scientific software
  - large language models
  - simulation configuration
  - provenance
  - PROV-O
  - SHACL
  - FAIR
  - reproducibility
